{
  "solution": "Summary of possibilities\n\n* \\(k=0\\) – always possible (all vertical lines).  \n* \\(k=1\\) – always possible (all vertical except one sunny line).  \n* \\(k=2\\) – impossible for any \\(n\\ge3\\) (proved in §1).  \n* \\(k=3\\) – possible for every \\(n\\ge4\\) by the construction of §4; for \\(n=3\\) a direct three‑sunny‑line covering (shown in the small‑case table) also works.  \n\nTherefore the set of admissible numbers of sunny lines is exactly  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\{0,\\;1,\\;3\\}} \\qquad\\text{for every integer } n\\ge 3 .\n\\]",
